+# Atlas conceptual model
+
+This canonical diagram set explains the supplied synthetic model in
+[the brief](../../brief.md). It describes conceptual relationships; no schema or
+application implementation exists. The three ownership roots are ORGANISATION,
+AGREEMENT and SERVICE. No relationships exist beyond those shown here.
+
+## Root overview
+
+How do the roots relate? Each agreement belongs to exactly one organisation and
+covers exactly one service. Organisations and services may each have no agreements.
+
+```mermaid
+erDiagram
+    ORGANISATION ||--o{ AGREEMENT : "has"
+    SERVICE ||--o{ AGREEMENT : "is covered by"
+```
+
+Read `||` as exactly one and `o{` as zero or more at the adjacent entity.
+The lines express the supplied associations and ownership; they do not specify
+keys or deletion behavior.
+
+Each root has compact detail in this document:
+
+- [ORGANISATION](#organisation) opens its owned detail.
+- [AGREEMENT](#agreement) opens its owned detail.
+- [SERVICE](#service) opens its owned detail.
+
+The detail views omit the root-to-root links already owned by this overview.
+
+## ORGANISATION
+
+What detail does an ORGANISATION own? Every child has exactly one ORGANISATION;
+an ORGANISATION may have zero or more of each child type.
+
+```mermaid
+erDiagram
+    ORGANISATION ||--o{ ADDRESS : "owns"
+    ORGANISATION ||--o{ CONTACT : "owns"
+    ORGANISATION ||--o{ IDENTIFIER : "owns"
+    ORGANISATION ||--o{ MEMBERSHIP : "owns"
+    ORGANISATION ||--o{ NOTE : "owns"
+```
+
+[Return to root overview](#root-overview).
+
+## AGREEMENT
+
+What detail does an AGREEMENT own? Every child has exactly one AGREEMENT;
+an AGREEMENT may have zero or more of each child type.
+
+```mermaid
+erDiagram
+    AGREEMENT ||--o{ CLAUSE : "owns"
+    AGREEMENT ||--o{ AMENDMENT : "owns"
+    AGREEMENT ||--o{ ATTACHMENT : "owns"
+    AGREEMENT ||--o{ MILESTONE : "owns"
+    AGREEMENT ||--o{ SIGNATURE : "owns"
+```
+
+[Return to root overview](#root-overview).
+
+## SERVICE
+
+What detail does a SERVICE own? Every child has exactly one SERVICE;
+a SERVICE may have zero or more of each child type.
+
+```mermaid
+erDiagram
+    SERVICE ||--o{ CATEGORY_ASSIGNMENT : "owns"
+    SERVICE ||--o{ OFFERING : "owns"
+    SERVICE ||--o{ REGION_ASSIGNMENT : "owns"
+    SERVICE ||--o{ SERVICE_NOTE : "owns"
+    SERVICE ||--o{ SERVICE_IDENTIFIER : "owns"
+```
+
+[Return to root overview](#root-overview).
+
+## Synthetic reasoning checks
+
+These examples exercise the supplied relationships without executing a schema.
+
+- **Find the service covered by an organisation's agreements.** Given organisation
+  O1 with agreements A1 and A2, both covering service S1, following
+  ORGANISATION → AGREEMENT → SERVICE returns S1 through both agreements. Multiple
+  agreements may cover the same service. An organisation O2 with no agreements
+  returns no services along this path.
+- **Find owned detail.** Given agreement A1 with clauses C1 and C2, following
+  AGREEMENT → CLAUSE returns both clauses. A2 with no clauses returns none.
+  Assigning C1 to both A1 and A2 would violate its exactly-one-owner rule. The
+  same cardinality check applies to every child type in the three detail views.
+- **Reject a missing root.** An agreement without an organisation or without a
+  service contradicts the overview. A service with no agreements is permitted.
+
+## Scope and verification
+
+The views account for all 18 entities and all 17 supplied relationships: two
+between roots and five owned-child relationships per root. All three overview
+roots are opened here, with each relationship drawn once. No attributes, keys,
+data types or lifecycle rules have been inferred.
+
+Source cardinalities, entity names, view sizes and local navigation were checked
+against the brief. No project renderer configuration or local `mmdc` command was
+found. Mermaid parsing, rendered readability and theme checks remain unperformed.
+No network, installation, application runtime or schema execution was used.
+
+PostgreSQL is selected in [project guidance](../../AGENTS.md); its representation
+is outside this conceptual task. A later implementation task would need explicit
+identity, attribute, key and lifecycle decisions before choosing that representation.
